"Initially, Leo came home exhausted and occasionally frustrated. Attempting to grasp foundational mathematics and science concepts in a language he was still acquiring required immense mental stamina. For several months, his English vocabulary appeared to lag slightly behind that of his monolingual peers, prompting anxious questions from well-meaning relatives who worried that dual-language instruction might confuse him or hinder his overall academic progress. Sofia herself momentarily wondered whether they had placed an unnecessary burden on their child’s shoulders.",
